{"step_index":1667,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T23:30:52Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-25T18:30:52-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T18:30:55-05:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-25T18:30:52-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T18:30:55-05:00\nShowing lines 120-443 of 443\n120:     %% Split off Swamped: Optional side cleanup vs. Mandatory Climax\n121:     M17 -.->|\"Optional Side Branch\"| M18[\"17. Don Gone<br/><code>COM_KBOS_CLEAN</code> • Clean Donnie's Trailer<br/>[ANY% SKIP / AUTO-FLAGGED]\"]\n122:     M18 -.-> M19[\"18. Recalibration<br/><code>HO_PAR_KEYCO</code> • Cal Grief Fishing<br/>[ANY% SKIP / AUTO-FLAGGED]\"]\n123:     \n124:     M17 ==>|\"Mandatory Story Spine\"| M20[\"19. Tourist Trap<br/><code>BIL_PICK</code> • Grassrivers Visitor Center<br/>[10:00–17:00 / 17:00–10:00]<br/>Dirty Cops Ambush — Jason Shot!\"]\n125:     M20 --> M21[\"20. Home Sweet Home<br/><code>BIL_HOUSE</code> • Lucia Solo Stash Retrieval<br/>Cartel Hitmen — House Burned Down!\"]\n126:     M21 --> M22[\"21. Discharge Time<br/><code>BIL_WHEEL</code> • VC Hospital Shootout<br/>★ CHAPTER 1 FINALE CLIMAX ★<br/>Ambulance Escape to Kelly County\"]\n127:     \n128:     M22 -->|\"Hard Transition\"| C2_Start[\"→ Chapter 2: What's in the Bag?<br/><code>MTL_WAKE</code> • Starlet Motel Arrival<br/>(func_10AA55 sweeps all 7 skipped side flags)\"]\n129: ```\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: ## 3. Chapter 2: Paradise Lost (Port Gellhorn & Kelly County)\n134: \n135: ### Mechanics & Structure\n136: - **Playable Character**: Heavily centered on **Lucia** during early recovery, then **permanently unlocks Dual Character Switching** via *\"Coffee Break\"*.\n137: - **Vehicle Fencing**: Unlocked via *\"Moses\"* (enabling Slim Jim vehicle thefts and custom garage registrations).\n138: - **Strict Chronological Sequence**: Organized into **4 sequential stages** that must be cleared in order (M23 through M44).\n139:   - **Stage 1: Motel Arrival & Medical (M23–M28)**: Infiltration, paying upkeep, Lucia solo medical run, and establishing fencing with Moses.\n140:   - **Stage 2: Debt Hustle & Gun Runs (M29–M37)**: Disguise setups, ambulance chasing, painkiller su\n<truncated 24313 bytes>\nion\n432: - A common misconception in player communities is that Ending A (*Bonnie & Clyde*) requires $2,000,000 in the player's bank account to unlock.\n433: - **Fact**: Script analysis confirms that **$2,000,000 is the mission completion cash reward** paid out to Jason and Lucia upon successfully surviving the Coast Guard gauntlet, NOT an entry prerequisite. Players do not need to grind money before initiating the finale.\n434: \n435: ### 3. Strict Sequential Progression vs. Concurrent Parallel Strands\n436: - **Chapters 2 & 4 (Sequential Stages)**: Visual \"wrap-around\" diagonal arrows in older community flowcharts made Chapters 2 and 4 look like parallel faction branches. In reality, they are strict chronological stages (Stages 1 through 4) where each phase must be fully cleared before the next stage opens.\n437: - **Chapter 3 (True Parallel Faction Strands)**: Once the Vice City safehouse is unlocked in Mission 50, Tyrone (Strand 1), Boobie (Strand 2), and Raul (Strand 3) are active simultaneously as concurrent map pins. Furthermore, the Sinfrontera Bank Heist features 3 concurrent preparation tracks (Safecracker, Explosives, Codes & Van) that can be tackled in any order.\n438: \n439: ### 4. Any% Speedrun Optimization Summary\n440: - **Chapter 1 Downtime Optimization**: Skip all 7 auto-flagged side missions (`Lab Fees`, `Unwanted Attention`, `Pipework`, `Hey Arnold!`, `Don Gone`, `Recalibration`, `Island Dreams`). The `MTL_WAKE` entry handler in `func_10AA55` automatically clears them for Any% completion!\n441: - **Skip All Social / Hot Meter Activities**: Ignore *Get Haircut*, *Buy Necklace*, *Buy Flowers*, *Buy Groceries*, and *Lucia's Clothes*.\n442: - **Save $75,000 Cash**: Keep at least $75,000 from the Sinfrontera Bank Heist ($10.5M take) to instantly bypass Abe Gonzalez's wire transfer gate in Chapter 4 (*Party Hard*).\n443: - **Select Ending B (*The Deal*)**: Accepting Mendez's immunity plea skips the multi-stage offshore Coast Guard gunboat battle, saving **8 to 12 minutes of real-world time** in Any% speedruns.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
